  const filePath = path.join(realBase, safeFilename);
  if (!filePath.startsWith(realBase)) throw new Error('Invalid file access');
  ```

- **Handle Errors Appropriately**: Instead of returning an empty string on error, consider throwing an error or returning a generic error message to avoid silent failures. This helps in identifying issues without exposing sensitive information.  
